[32m│[0m [4;35m1  Scope and Purpose[0m                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m This specification defines the mandatory incoming inspection, electrical acceptance tests, and LED [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m chromaticity/photometric tests required to validate every production unit of the MDIO-INPUT1 PCB   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m assembly prior to shipment or integration into end systems.                                        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m The MDIO-INPUT1 is a 16-channel, 24 V DC digital input module intended for use in industrial       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m automation and process-control environments. Its primary function is to receive field-side digital [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m signals in the 24 V range, provide galvanic isolation via quad optocouplers, and report the logic  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m states over a standard I²C bus using a PCF8575 16bit port expander. Two physical I²C connection    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m options (pin header and flat cable/IDC) are provided.                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m All tests documented herein apply to Class 2 performance per IPC-A-610 unless otherwise stated.    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m Tests are mandatory and must be completed in the sequence given. A unit that fails any test is     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m quarantined and dispositioned before it may proceed to subsequent tests.                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                    [32m│[0m
